 * License. You may obtain a copy of the License at
 *
 * http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
 *
 * Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS"
 * BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied. See the License for the specific language
 * governing permissions and limitations under the License.
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Owns the lifecycle of a suspended-for-approval tool call once a gateway is
 * presenting it: creates and tracks the AgentSuspension, and resolves it exactly
 * once with a human's decision.
 *
 * This does NOT replace AiAgent's existing checkpoint/resume mechanism — the
 * suspension here just points at a checkpoint (by threadID) the way AgentSuspension
 * itself documents. It exists so the SAME pending approval can be safely presented
 * to (and resolved from) more than one gateway without double-resolving — e.g. the
 * same approval mirrored to both a web UI and Slack, where either channel might
 * answer first.
 *
 * Concurrency: the atomic claim on an AgentSuspension's status uses
 * java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap.replace(), a real compare-and-set — of two
 * simultaneous resolve() calls for the same suspension, exactly one succeeds and
 * the other throws SuspensionAlreadyResolved. That guarantee is scoped to a single
 * coordinator instance/process — see the durability note below for what that means
 * once suspensions can also be loaded into a fresh instance after a restart.
 *
 * Durability: suspensions, their meta, and their eventual decision are, when a
 * checkpointer is linked (see setCheckpointer() — HumanInTheLoopMiddleware wires this
 * automatically via its onAttach() hook), persisted through the SAME IAiMemory-shaped
 * store AiAgent already checkpoints turns to — under a distinct key namespace, not
 * overlapping AiAgent's own threadId-keyed entries. A fresh coordinator (e.g. after a
 * restart) transparently hydrates a suspension from that store the first time it's
 * looked up or resolved, rather than only ever knowing about suspensions it created
 * itself. This closes the previous gap where a checkpoint could survive a restart
 * while this coordinator's own bookkeeping — kept only in memory — did not.
 * "approve_session" grants are the one exception: they're deliberately NEVER
 * persisted (see sessionGrants below) — that's unchanged by any of this.
 * Note the atomic-claim guarantee above does NOT extend across two coordinator
 * instances resolving the same hydrated suspension concurrently (e.g. two separate
 * processes racing) — each instance's compare-and-set is only atomic within itself.
 * Treat cross-process concurrent resolution as out of scope for this phase.
 *
 * Bulk/durable lookups (hasPending/getAllPending/clearSuspension/clearAllPending): backed
 * by a single well-known checkpointer key (see pendingIndexKey()) holding every currently-
 * pending suspensionID, rather than a real prefix-scan of the checkpointer — deliberately,
 * since IAiMemory has no such capability and most backends don't durably persist
 * saveState/loadState/clearState at all beyond Cache/File/Jdbc. That single key is
 * read-modified-written on every create/resolve/clear, so two processes racing on it can
 * each miss the other's update. The failure mode is self-correcting for false positives
 * (a stale "still pending" entry — getAllPending() re-checks each suspension's actual
 * persisted status before returning it, and the atomic claim in resolve() still prevents
 * a real double-resolve regardless). It is NOT self-correcting for a false negative — a
 * suspension whose creation crashed between persistSuspension() and addToPendingIndex()
 * would never appear in getAllPending() at all. Treat that as out of scope for this phase,
 * same as the cross-process atomicity gap above.
 *
 * Sharper version of that same caveat, worth knowing before choosing a checkpointer: the
 * pending index is scoped ONLY by its fixed key, not by anything identifying this
 * coordinator/agent — so two coordinators that happen to share a checkpointer resolving to
 * the SAME underlying store see one COMBINED index, not two separate ones. In the common
 * one-agent-per-checkpointer usage this never comes up. It's easy to hit by accident,
 * though: CacheMemory's saveState/loadState/clearState key purely by threadId
 * ("checkpoint:" & threadId, see CacheMemory.buildCheckpointKey()) — NOT by that
 * CacheMemory instance's own `key` — so every `aiMemory("cache")` call anywhere in the
 * same runtime shares one checkpoint keyspace regardless of how many separate instances
 * you construct. Suspension-scoped keys (persistenceKey(), keyed by a UUID) don't collide
 * in practice even when that keyspace is shared; this one fixed index key does. Give each
 * logically-distinct coordinator/agent a genuinely isolated store (e.g. a File-backed
 * memory pointed at its own directory) if you need separate pending indexes.
 *
 * Decision settled for Phase 2: invalid edited arguments (failing validation
 * against the tool's declared schema) do NOT throw and do NOT re-suspend for
 * correction. They're normalized into a REJECTED outcome with a reason describing
 * what failed — consistent with how "reject" already behaves everywhere else in
 * this module (soft-skip the tool call, keep the run going). Re-suspending for
 * in-place correction is a reasonable future enhancement but adds a retry loop this
 * phase doesn't need.
 *
 * @since 4.0.0
 */
import bxModules.bxai.models.gateway.IGateway;
import bxModules.bxai.models.gateway.AgentSuspension;
import bxModules.bxai.models.gateway.contracts.GatewayContext;
import bxModules.bxai.models.gateway.contracts.HumanInteractionRequest;
import bxModules.bxai.models.gateway.contracts.HumanInteractionDecision;
import bxModules.bxai.models.hitl.decisions.IDecisionStore;
import bxModules.bxai.models.tools.ITool;

class {

	/**
	 * Pending/resolved suspensions, keyed by suspensionID
	 */
	property name="suspensions" type="struct" default={};

	/**
	 * The decision each resolved suspension was resolved with, keyed by suspensionID
	 */
	property name="decisions" type="struct" default={};

	/**
	 * java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap<String,String> of suspensionID -> status,
	 * used purely as the atomic compare-and-set primitive for resolve()
	 */
	property name="statusLocks";

	/**
	 * Optional durable grant store for "approve_always" decisions. When absent, "approve_always"
	 * behaves identically to "approve_session" — a per-coordinator, in-memory grant only.
	 */
	property name="decisionStore";

	/**
	 * Optional durable store for suspension/decision state (see setCheckpointer()). When absent,
	 * suspensions live only in this coordinator's in-memory structs, as before this existed.
	 */
	property name="checkpointer";

	/**
	 * "approve_session" grants, in-memory only, keyed by "threadID:toolName". Deliberately not
	 * backed by IDecisionStore — a session grant should never outlive this coordinator.
	 */
	property name="sessionGrants" type="struct" default={};

	/**
	 * Identity/toolName captured at requestApproval() time so resolve() — which only sees a
	 * suspensionID and a decision — can still record a grant when the decision calls for one.
	 * Keyed by suspensionID.
	 */
	property name="suspensionMeta" type="struct" default={};

	/**
	 * Constructor
	 *
	 * @decisionStore Optional IDecisionStore for durable "approve_always" grants
	 */
	function init( IDecisionStore decisionStore ) {
		variables.suspensions   = {}
		variables.decisions     = {}
		variables.statusLocks   = createObject( "java", "java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap" ).init()
		variables.decisionStore = arguments.decisionStore ?: javacast( "null", "" )
		variables.sessionGrants = {}
		variables.suspensionMeta = {}
		return this;
	}

	/**
	 * Link a durable store for suspension/decision state, so a suspension created by this
	 * coordinator can still be found and resolved by another instance later — e.g. after a
	 * restart. Typically wired automatically by HumanInTheLoopMiddleware.onAttach() from the
	 * agent's own checkpointer; call directly only for a coordinator built without a
	 * middleware/agent in the picture.
	 *
	 * @checkpointer Any IAiMemory instance supporting saveState/loadState/clearState
	 *
	 * @return This coordinator for chaining
	 */
	HumanInteractionCoordinator function setCheckpointer( required any checkpointer ) {
		variables.checkpointer = arguments.checkpointer
		return this;
	}

	/**
	 * Present a HumanInteractionRequest to a human via the given gateway, creating and
	 * tracking an AgentSuspension for it.
	 *
	 * If an identity/tool pair already carries a durable ("approve_always") or in-session
	 * ("approve_session") grant, the suspension is created but never presented — it's
	 * auto-resolved as approved immediately, same as a synchronous gateway's instant decision.
	 *
	 * For synchronous gateways (the delivery already carries a decision — see
	 * GatewayDeliveryResult.hasDecision()), the suspension is resolved immediately and
	 * returned already in its terminal state. For asynchronous gateways, the suspension
	 * is returned still pending; call resolve() later when the decision arrives.
	 *
	 * @humanRequest The interaction request to present
	 * @context      The GatewayContext identifying who/where to present it to
	 * @gateway      The gateway to present the request through
	 * @executionID  The agent execution/run this suspension correlates to
	 * @threadID     The checkpointed thread this suspension can be resumed from
	 * @checkpoint   Opaque checkpoint reference/metadata
	 * @tool         The tool being called, if known — used to validate an immediate "edit" decision
	 *
	 * @return The AgentSuspension tracking this request
	 */
	AgentSuspension function requestApproval(
		required HumanInteractionRequest humanRequest,
		required GatewayContext context,
		required IGateway gateway,
		string executionID = "",
		string threadID    = "",
		struct checkpoint  = {},
		ITool tool
	) {
		var toolName = !isNull( arguments.tool ) ? arguments.tool.getName() : ( arguments.humanRequest.getPendingAction().toolName ?: "" )
		var identity = arguments.context.getUserID()

		var suspension = new AgentSuspension(
			executionID: arguments.executionID,
			threadID   : arguments.threadID,
			reason     : arguments.humanRequest.getMessage(),
			interaction: arguments.humanRequest,
			checkpoint : arguments.checkpoint
		)

		variables.statusLocks.put( suspension.getSuspensionID(), AgentSuspension.STATUSES.PENDING )
		variables.suspensions[ suspension.getSuspensionID() ] = suspension
		variables.suspensionMeta[ suspension.getSuspensionID() ] = {
			"identity": identity,
			"toolName": toolName,
			"threadID": arguments.threadID
		}
		persistSuspension( suspension.getSuspensionID() )
		addToPendingIndex( suspension.getSuspensionID() )

		if ( len( toolName ) && isAlreadyGranted( identity, arguments.threadID, toolName ) ) {
			var autoDecision = new HumanInteractionDecision(
				requestID: arguments.humanRequest.getId(),
				decision : HumanInteractionDecision.DECISIONS.APPROVE,
				reason   : "Auto-approved via an existing grant.",
				decidedBy: identity
			)
			resolve( suspension.getSuspensionID(), autoDecision, arguments.tool )
			return suspension
		}

		var delivery = arguments.gateway.requestHumanInteraction( arguments.humanRequest, arguments.context )

		if ( delivery.hasDecision() ) {
			resolve( suspension.getSuspensionID(), delivery.getDecision(), arguments.tool )
		}

		return suspension
	}

	/**
	 * Resolve a pending suspension with a human's decision. Atomic — see class docs.
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The AgentSuspension.suspensionID to resolve
	 * @decision     The human's decision
	 * @tool         The tool being called, if known — used to validate an "edit" decision's arguments
	 *
	 * @throws SuspensionNotFound        if no pending suspension exists with that id
	 * @throws SuspensionAlreadyResolved if another resolve() call already claimed it
	 *
	 * @return The now-resolved AgentSuspension
	 */
	AgentSuspension function resolve(
		required string suspensionID,
		required HumanInteractionDecision decision,
		ITool tool
	) {
		hydrateSuspension( arguments.suspensionID )

		if ( !variables.suspensions.keyExists( arguments.suspensionID ) ) {
			throw(
				type   : "SuspensionNotFound",
				message: "No pending suspension with id [#arguments.suspensionID#]."
			)
		}

		var suspension  = variables.suspensions[ arguments.suspensionID ]
		var decision    = arguments.decision
		var newStatus   = decisionToStatus( decision )

		// Validate edited arguments BEFORE claiming — a validation failure downgrades
		// the effective decision to a rejection instead of applying bad arguments.
		// editedData may be the raw args struct directly, or wrapped as { correctedArgs: {...} }
		// (the convention documented on HumanInteractionDecision.editedData and used by
		// HumanInTheLoopMiddleware's resume path) — unwrap the same way before validating.
		if ( decision.isEdit() && !isNull( arguments.tool ) ) {
			var editedArgs       = decision.getEditedData().correctedArgs ?: decision.getEditedData()
			var validationError = validateArguments( arguments.tool, editedArgs )
			if ( !isNull( validationError ) ) {
				decision = new HumanInteractionDecision(
					requestID: decision.getRequestID(),
					decision : "reject",
					reason   : validationError,
					decidedBy: decision.getDecidedBy()
				)
				newStatus = AgentSuspension.STATUSES.REJECTED
			}
		}

		var claimed = variables.statusLocks.replace(
			arguments.suspensionID,
			AgentSuspension.STATUSES.PENDING,
			newStatus
		)

		if ( !claimed ) {
			throw(
				type   : "SuspensionAlreadyResolved",
				message: "Suspension [#arguments.suspensionID#] was already resolved with status [#variables.statusLocks.get( arguments.suspensionID )#]."
			)
		}

		suspension.setStatus( newStatus )
		variables.decisions[ arguments.suspensionID ] = decision

		if ( decision.isApprovedAlways() || decision.isApprovedForSession() ) {
			recordGrant( arguments.suspensionID, decision )
		}

		persistSuspension( arguments.suspensionID )
		removeFromPendingIndex( arguments.suspensionID )

		return suspension
	}

	/**
	 * Whether a suspension is currently tracked as pending in the durable index. Cheap —
	 * checks the index only, without hydrating the full suspension. False for an unknown
	 * id, a resolved suspension, or when no checkpointer is linked (nothing durable to
	 * check — falls back to false rather than an in-memory-only guess).
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension id to check
	 */
	boolean function hasPending( required string suspensionID ) {
		var targetID = arguments.suspensionID
		return !loadPendingIndex().filter( ( id ) => id == targetID ).isEmpty()
	}

	/**
	 * Every currently-pending suspension, per the durable index. Hydrates any suspension
	 * not already in memory (same as getSuspension()), then re-checks each one's actual
	 * persisted status before including it — the index can go stale (see class docs), the
	 * suspension's own status is the real source of truth.
	 *
	 * @return Array of pending AgentSuspension instances
	 */
	array function getAllPending() {
		return loadPendingIndex()
			.map( ( id ) => getSuspension( id ) )
			.filter( ( suspension ) => !isNull( suspension ) && suspension.isPending() )
	}

	/**
	 * Remove a suspension entirely — from the durable index, its own durable entry, and
	 * this coordinator's in-memory structs. Distinct from resolve(): this doesn't require
	 * or record a decision, it just forgets the suspension ever existed. Intended for
	 * administrative cleanup (an expired or abandoned request), not a human decision path.
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension to clear
	 */
	void function clearSuspension( required string suspensionID ) {
		clearSuspensionEntry( arguments.suspensionID )
		removeFromPendingIndex( arguments.suspensionID )
	}

	/**
	 * Clear every currently-pending suspension — see clearSuspension(). An administrative
	 * bulk reset (tests, or an operator flushing a stuck queue), not a decision path.
	 */
	void function clearAllPending() {
		var ids = loadPendingIndex()
		ids.each( ( id ) => clearSuspensionEntry( id ) )
		savePendingIndex( [] )
	}

	/**
	 * Look up a tracked suspension by id, pending or resolved. Transparently hydrates it
	 * from the linked checkpointer first if this coordinator instance doesn't already have
	 * it in memory (see class docs on durability).
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The AgentSuspension.suspensionID to look up
	 */
	AgentSuspension function getSuspension( required string suspensionID ) {
		hydrateSuspension( arguments.suspensionID )
		return variables.suspensions[ arguments.suspensionID ] ?: javacast( "null", "" )
	}

	/**
	 * Look up the decision a suspension was resolved with, if any. Transparently hydrates
	 * from the linked checkpointer first — see getSuspension().
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The AgentSuspension.suspensionID to look up
	 */
	HumanInteractionDecision function getDecision( required string suspensionID ) {
		hydrateSuspension( arguments.suspensionID )
		return variables.decisions[ arguments.suspensionID ] ?: javacast( "null", "" )
	}

	/**
	 * Map a HumanInteractionDecision to the AgentSuspension status it resolves to.
	 *
	 * @decision The decision to map
	 */
	private string function decisionToStatus( required HumanInteractionDecision decision ) {
		if ( arguments.decision.isApproved() ) {
			return AgentSuspension.STATUSES.APPROVED
		}
		if ( arguments.decision.isRejected() ) {
			return AgentSuspension.STATUSES.REJECTED
		}
		if ( arguments.decision.isEdit() ) {
			return AgentSuspension.STATUSES.EDITED
		}
		if ( arguments.decision.isCancelled() ) {
			return AgentSuspension.STATUSES.CANCELLED
		}
		return AgentSuspension.STATUSES.FAILED
	}

	/**
	 * Whether the given identity already holds a grant — durable ("approve_always", via
	 * decisionStore) or in-session ("approve_session", via sessionGrants) — for this tool on
	 * this thread. A missing identity or toolName can never be granted.
	 *
	 * @identity Who is asking
	 * @threadID The thread the session grant (if any) would be scoped to
	 * @toolName The tool being called
	 */
	private boolean function isAlreadyGranted( required string identity, required string threadID, required string toolName ) {
		if ( !len( arguments.identity ) || !len( arguments.toolName ) ) {
			return false
		}

		if ( variables.sessionGrants.keyExists( sessionGrantKey( arguments.threadID, arguments.toolName ) ) ) {
			return true
		}

		if ( !isNull( variables.decisionStore ) ) {
			return variables.decisionStore.isGranted( arguments.identity, arguments.toolName )
		}

		return false
	}

	/**
	 * Record a grant after a suspension resolves with "approve_always"/"approve_session",
	 * looking up the identity/toolName captured at requestApproval() time since resolve()
	 * itself only sees a suspensionID.
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension that just resolved
	 * @decision     The decision it resolved with
	 */
	private void function recordGrant( required string suspensionID, required HumanInteractionDecision decision ) {
		var meta = variables.suspensionMeta[ arguments.suspensionID ] ?: javacast( "null", "" )
		if ( isNull( meta ) || !len( meta.identity ) || !len( meta.toolName ) ) {
			return
		}

		if ( arguments.decision.isApprovedForSession() ) {
			variables.sessionGrants[ sessionGrantKey( meta.threadID, meta.toolName ) ] = true
			return
		}

		if ( arguments.decision.isApprovedAlways() && !isNull( variables.decisionStore ) ) {
			variables.decisionStore.grant( meta.identity, meta.toolName )
		}
	}

	/**
	 * Build the sessionGrants key for a thread/tool pair.
	 *
	 * @threadID The thread a session grant is scoped to
	 * @toolName The tool the grant applies to
	 */
	private string function sessionGrantKey( required string threadID, required string toolName ) {
		return arguments.threadID & ":" & arguments.toolName
	}

	/**
	 * Validate edited arguments against a tool's declared schema (OpenAI function-schema
	 * shape: { function: { parameters: { properties, required, additionalProperties } } },
	 * or a bare { parameters: {...} }/{ properties: {...} } shape).
	 *
	 * @tool        The tool the edited arguments would be invoked with
	 * @editedArgs  The human-edited arguments struct to validate
	 *
	 * @return null if valid, otherwise a human-readable description of what failed
	 */
	private any function validateArguments( required ITool tool, required struct editedArgs ) {
		var schema     = arguments.tool.getSchema()
		var fn         = schema.function ?: schema
		var params     = fn.parameters ?: {}
		var required   = params.required ?: []
		var properties = params.properties ?: {}
		var editedArgs = arguments.editedArgs

		var missing = required.filter( ( key ) => !editedArgs.keyExists( key ) )
		if ( missing.len() ) {
			return "Edited arguments are missing required field(s): [#missing.toList()#]."
		}

		if ( params.keyExists( "additionalProperties" ) && !params.additionalProperties && !properties.isEmpty() ) {
			var unknown = editedArgs.keyArray().filter( ( key ) => !properties.keyExists( key ) )
			if ( unknown.len() ) {
				return "Edited arguments contain field(s) not in the tool's schema: [#unknown.toList()#]."
			}
		}

		return javacast( "null", "" )
	}

	/**
	 * Persist a suspension (plus its meta and, once resolved, its decision) through the
	 * linked checkpointer. A no-op when no checkpointer is linked. Called after every
	 * state change (creation and resolution) so the durable copy never lags behind what's
	 * in memory.
	 *
	 * Stored as plain structs (not the live AgentSuspension/HumanInteractionDecision
	 * objects) — the same discipline AiAgent's own checkpointing follows, since a File/Jdbc
	 * -backed store needs to serialize this, not hold a live object reference.
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension to persist
	 */
	private void function persistSuspension( required string suspensionID ) {
		if ( isNull( variables.checkpointer ) ) {
			return
		}

		var suspension = variables.suspensions[ arguments.suspensionID ] ?: javacast( "null", "" )
		if ( isNull( suspension ) ) {
			return
		}
		var decision = variables.decisions[ arguments.suspensionID ] ?: javacast( "null", "" )

		variables.checkpointer.saveState(
			persistenceKey( arguments.suspensionID ),
			{
				"suspension": suspension.toStruct(),
				"meta"      : variables.suspensionMeta[ arguments.suspensionID ] ?: {},
				"decision"  : isNull( decision ) ? {} : decision.toStruct()
			}
		)
	}

	/**
	 * Load a suspension into this coordinator's in-memory structs from the linked
	 * checkpointer, if this instance doesn't already have it — e.g. a fresh coordinator
	 * after a restart, being asked to resolve a suspension a previous instance created.
	 * A no-op when no checkpointer is linked, or the suspension is already in memory, or
	 * nothing durable is found under that id.
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension to hydrate
	 */
	private void function hydrateSuspension( required string suspensionID ) {
		if ( variables.suspensions.keyExists( arguments.suspensionID ) || isNull( variables.checkpointer ) ) {
			return
		}

		var saved = variables.checkpointer.loadState( persistenceKey( arguments.suspensionID ) )
		if ( saved.isEmpty() ) {
			return
		}

		var suspension = structToSuspension( saved.suspension )
		variables.suspensions[ arguments.suspensionID ]    = suspension
		variables.suspensionMeta[ arguments.suspensionID ] = saved.meta ?: {}
		variables.statusLocks.putIfAbsent( arguments.suspensionID, suspension.getStatus() )

		if ( !isNull( saved.decision ) && !saved.decision.isEmpty() ) {
			variables.decisions[ arguments.suspensionID ] = new HumanInteractionDecision( argumentCollection: saved.decision )
		}
	}

	/**
	 * The checkpointer key a suspension is persisted under — distinct from AiAgent's own
	 * threadId-keyed checkpoint entries so the two never collide in a shared store.
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension id to build a key for
	 */
	private string function persistenceKey( required string suspensionID ) {
		return "hitl:suspension:" & arguments.suspensionID
	}

	/**
	 * The single, well-known checkpointer key the durable pending-suspension index is
	 * stored under. See class docs for why this is one key rather than a real prefix-scan.
	 */
	private string function pendingIndexKey() {
		return "hitl:pending-index"
	}

	/**
	 * Load the current durable set of pending suspensionIDs. Always reads straight from
	 * the checkpointer rather than caching in memory — these bulk operations exist
	 * specifically to see durable, possibly cross-process state. Empty array when no
	 * checkpointer is linked or nothing has been indexed yet.
	 */
	private array function loadPendingIndex() {
		if ( isNull( variables.checkpointer ) ) {
			return []
		}
		var saved = variables.checkpointer.loadState( pendingIndexKey() )
		return saved.ids ?: []
	}

	/**
	 * Persist the given set of pending suspensionIDs as the durable index. A no-op when no
	 * checkpointer is linked.
	 *
	 * @ids The full set of currently-pending suspensionIDs to persist
	 */
	private void function savePendingIndex( required array ids ) {
		if ( isNull( variables.checkpointer ) ) {
			return
		}
		variables.checkpointer.saveState( pendingIndexKey(), { "ids": arguments.ids } )
	}

	/**
	 * Add a suspensionID to the durable pending index. A no-op when no checkpointer is
	 * linked, or it's already present.
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension to add
	 */
	private void function addToPendingIndex( required string suspensionID ) {
		if ( isNull( variables.checkpointer ) ) {
			return
		}
		var targetID = arguments.suspensionID
		var ids      = loadPendingIndex()
		if ( ids.filter( ( id ) => id == targetID ).isEmpty() ) {
			ids.append( targetID )
			savePendingIndex( ids )
		}
	}

	/**
	 * Remove a suspensionID from the durable pending index. A no-op when no checkpointer
	 * is linked.
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension to remove
	 */
	private void function removeFromPendingIndex( required string suspensionID ) {
		if ( isNull( variables.checkpointer ) ) {
			return
		}
		var targetID = arguments.suspensionID
		savePendingIndex( loadPendingIndex().filter( ( id ) => id != targetID ) )
	}

	/**
	 * Delete a single suspension's own durable entry and in-memory bookkeeping — everything
	 * except its membership in the pending index, which clearSuspension()/clearAllPending()
	 * handle separately (clearAllPending() batches the index write into one, rather than
	 * once per suspension).
	 *
	 * @suspensionID The suspension entry to delete
	 */
	private void function clearSuspensionEntry( required string suspensionID ) {
		if ( !isNull( variables.checkpointer ) ) {
			variables.checkpointer.clearState( persistenceKey( arguments.suspensionID ) )
		}
		variables.suspensions.delete( arguments.suspensionID )
		variables.decisions.delete( arguments.suspensionID )
		variables.suspensionMeta.delete( arguments.suspensionID )
		variables.statusLocks.remove( arguments.suspensionID )
	}

	/**
	 * Reconstruct an AgentSuspension from AgentSuspension.toStruct()'s projection. Only the
	 * nested `interaction` needs special handling — it comes back as a plain struct (from
	 * HumanInteractionRequest.toStruct()) rather than flattened, so it's rebuilt into a real
	 * HumanInteractionRequest before the rest round-trips via argumentCollection.
	 */
	private AgentSuspension function structToSuspension( required struct data ) {
		var interaction = ( !isNull( arguments.data.interaction ) && isStruct( arguments.data.interaction ) )
			? new HumanInteractionRequest( argumentCollection: arguments.data.interaction )
			: javacast( "null", "" )

		return new AgentSuspension(
			suspensionID: arguments.data.suspensionID,
			executionID : arguments.data.executionID,
			threadID    : arguments.data.threadID,
			reason      : arguments.data.reason,
			status      : arguments.data.status,
			interaction : interaction,
			checkpoint  : arguments.data.checkpoint,
			createdAt   : arguments.data.createdAt,
			expiresAt   : arguments.data.expiresAt ?: javacast( "null", "" )
		)
	}

}
